# In an organisation these would be team handles (@org/platform,
# @org/platform-leads, @org/security) with different groups owning different
# paths. This repository has a single maintainer, so the paths below record
# *which* areas warrant a second pair of eyes rather than enforcing who.
#
# Required-approvals is deliberately not enabled in branch protection: GitHub
# does not let an author approve their own pull request, and a single-
# maintainer repository would deadlock on every change.

*                       @zelkourban

# Shared modules change all three environments at once.
/modules/               @zelkourban

# Production configuration and the pipelines themselves are the two places
# where a mistake is expensive and hard to undo.
/envs/prod/             @zelkourban
/.github/workflows/     @zelkourban
/bootstrap/             @zelkourban
